    {
      "ts": 1786406468806,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "unzip and perl installed. The Walnut Creek CD doesn't have pov files in the index. Let me try fetching the full file listing and also try other known archive sources for POV-Ray 2.2."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786406468806,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_1d3256862e704b54a3156d40",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "cd /tmp\necho \"=== full Walnut Creek file listing, grep pov ===\"\ncurl -s --max-time 40 \"https://archive.org/metadata/Linux_Games_CD-ROM_Walnut_Creek_July_1999/files\" -o wc_files.json 2>&1\necho \"size: $(wc -c < wc_files.json) bytes\"\n# parse with grep for any pov mentions\ngrep -io '[^\"]*pov[^\"]*' wc_files.json 2>/dev/null | sort -u | head -40"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786406470228,
      "type": "tool_result",
      "call_id": "call_1d3256862e704b54a3156d40",
      "output": {
        "ok": {
          "content": "=== full Walnut Creek file listing, grep pov ===\nsize: 2744 bytes\n\n[exit code: 0]\n\nnote: this cd'd to `/tmp`, outside the session root `/app`. Only work under the session root is collected when the turn finishes — every other tool is confined to it, so edits under `/tmp` are invisible to the file tools, to this turn's diff, and to verification. graph_query and the grep/glob code-map footers index only this root, so it isn't covered by the code graph either. To work on that tree, re-root the session on it (run stella from it)."
        }
      },
