    {
      "ts": 1786406571300,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This is exactly what I need. The ibiblio `rays/pov/` directory has POV-Ray 2.2 source archives. The README explains the build: edit `INSTBIN=` in the Makefile, then `make install?` (s/x/v). \n\nKey observation: the sanity check uses `+L/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include`, so the include files (shapes.inc, colors.inc, textures.inc) must end up at that path. Let me set up tasks and download the archives."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786406571300,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_c62bf5abfcff4de886e2e1ba",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "cd /tmp\necho \"=== Downloading POV-Ray 2.2 archives from ibiblio ===\"\nBASE=\"https://www.ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/apps/graphics/rays/pov/\"\nfor f in povsrc-2.2.tar.gz povinc-2.2.tar.gz povdoc-2.2.tar.gz povscn-2.2.tar.gz; do\n  echo \"--- downloading $f ---\"\n  curl -sS --max-time 60 -o \"$f\" \"${BASE}${f}\"\n  echo \"  size: $(wc -c < $f) bytes\"\ndone\necho \"=== verify they are gzip ===\"\nfile povsrc-2.2.tar.gz povinc-2.2.tar.gz povdoc-2.2.tar.gz povscn-2.2.tar.gz 2>/dev/null || (for f in povsrc-2.2.tar.gz povinc-2.2.tar.gz povdoc-2.2.tar.gz povscn-2.2.tar.gz; do echo -n \"$f: \"; head -c2 \"$f\" | xxd | head -1; done)"
        }
      }
    },
