    {
      "ts": 1786406668240,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The test scene `illum1.pov` is actually one of POV-Ray 2.2's own sample scenes (`scenes/level2/illum1.pov`), confirming version 2.2 is correct. \n\nNow about the include path. The sanity command path `/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include` is interesting. Looking at the official POV-Team distribution: the archives were named `povsrc.tar.Z`, `povscn.tar.Z`, `povdoc.tar.Z` — where `povdoc.tar.Z` originally contained `doc/` AND `include/` together (the README says \"If you haven't... you should probably only get the new source or binary archive, as the docs, include, and scene files are unchanged\"). The Linux porter split include into a separate `povinc` archive, but in the official distribution the include files lived under the `povdoc` umbrella.\n\nThe grader explicitly uses `+L/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include`, so I must ensure the include files exist at that path. I'll create a `povdoc` directory with `include/` populated. Let me set up the layout and then tackle the build. First, let me create a task list and attempt the compile to see what breaks with modern gcc."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786406668240,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_6704dcfc3b0640d1adc73a42",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "# Create the povdoc layout the sanity command expects:\n# +L/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include  -> must contain shapes.inc, colors.inc, textures.inc\nmkdir -p /app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include\ncp -a /app/povray-2.2/pov/include/* /app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include/\n# Also copy doc into povdoc to mirror the official povdoc archive layout\ncp -a /app/povray-2.2/pov/doc /app/povray-2.2/povdoc/ 2>/dev/null\necho \"=== povdoc/include now has ===\"\nls /app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include/ | grep -E 'shapes.inc|colors.inc|textures.inc'\necho \"=== verify count ===\"\nls /app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include/ | wc -l"
        }
      }
    },
