          "content": "object files:  povray.o bezier.o blob.o bound.o boxes.o camera.o colour.o cones.o csg.o discs.o dump.o express.o gif.o gifdecod.o hfield.o iff.o image.o lighting.o matrices.o normal.o objects.o parse.o pigment.o planes.o point.o poly.o quadrics.o raw.o ray.o render.o spheres.o targa.o texture.o tokenize.o triangle.o txttest.o vect.o unix.o\n=== Link ===\n=== link exit: 0 ===\n-rwxrwxrwx. 1 root root 308792 Aug 11 00:05 /tmp/povray_test\n=== run ===\n\n  Persistence of Vision Raytracer Ver 2.2linux386\n    This is an unofficial version compiled by:\n     Jeff Epler (jepler@herbie.unl.edu)\n     The POV-Ray Team is not responsible for supporting this version.\n  Copyright 1993 POV-Team\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  POV-Ray is based on DKBTrace 2.12 by David K. Buck & Aaron A. Collins.\n    Contributing Authors: (Alphabetically)\n       Steve Anger        Steve A. Bennett   David K. Buck\n       Aaron A. Collins   Alexander Enzmann  Dan Farmer\n       Douglas Muir       Bill Pulver        Robert Skinner\n       Scott Taylor       Drew Wells         Chris Young\n    Other contributors listed in the documentation.\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nUsage: POVRAY  [+/-] Option1 [+/-] Option2 ...\n  Example: +L\\povray\\include +Iscene.pov +Oscene.tga +W320 +H200\n  Example: +Iscene.pov +Oscene.tga +W160 +H200 +V -D +X \n\n\n[exit code: 0]\n\nnote: this cd'd to `/tmp`, outside the session root `/app`. Only work under the session root is collected when the turn finishes — every other tool is confined to it, so edits under `/tmp` are invisible to the file tools, to this turn's diff, and to verification. graph_query and the grep/glob code-map footers index only this root, so it isn't covered by the code graph either. To work on that tree, re-root the session on it (run stella from it)."
