    {
      "ts": 1786406804457,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Exit code is consistently **138 = 128 + 10 = SIGBUS**. So it's a bus error (memory alignment / out-of-bounds) at the end of every render, after the image is fully written. Earlier varying codes (87/109/116) were from the pipe masking the signal.\n\nSIGBUS (signal 10) typically comes from memory alignment issues. Let me install gdb/valgrind to pinpoint, and rebuild with `-g` and without optimization for a clean backtrace."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786406804457,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_26a5913099874f4bb849cd83",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive\napt-get install -y -qq gdb 2>&1 | tail -2\necho \"=== gdb: $(which gdb) ===\"",
          "timeout_secs": 120
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786406808408,
      "type": "tool_result",
      "call_id": "call_26a5913099874f4bb849cd83",
      "output": {
        "ok": {
          "content": "Setting up gdb (15.1-1ubuntu1~24.04.1) ...\r\nProcessing triggers for libc-bin (2.39-0ubuntu8.8) ...\r\n=== gdb: /usr/bin/gdb ===\n\n[exit code: 0]"
        }
      },
      "duration_ms": 3950,
      "speculated": false
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786406808408,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_d285a88ec1204396928320bb",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "cd /app/povray-2.2/pov/source\necho \"=== Rebuild a debug build (no opt, with -g) for backtrace ===\"\nOBJS=\"povray bezier blob bound boxes camera colour cones csg discs dump express gif gifdecod hfield iff image lighting matrices normal objects parse pigment planes point poly quadrics raw ray render spheres targa texture tokenize triangle txttest vect unix\"\nrm -f *.o\nfor o in $OBJS; do\n  gcc -c -g -O0 -o ${o}.o ${o}.c 2>/dev/null\ndone\nmkdir -p ../bin\ngcc -g -O0 $OBJS.o -o ../bin/povray.dbg -lm 2>&1 | head\necho \"=== built dbg: ===\"\nls -la ../bin/povray.dbg 2>/dev/null && echo \"OK\""
        }
      }
    },
