    {
      "ts": 1786406834647,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The `-O0` build **exits cleanly (0) every time**. The crash only happens with `-O2`. So this is an optimization-dependent bug — `-ffast-math` and aggressive optimizations break the 1993 code. The safe fix is to build without `-ffast-math` and with conservative optimization. Let me figure out which flag triggers it. First test `-O0` works fully (the real test image), then narrow down the optimization flags.\n\nThe debug build works. But I want a properly-working optimized build. Let me determine the minimal flag change. Let me test `-O2` without `-ffast-math`."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786406834647,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_933223be2af24d4a94e9365d",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "cd /app/povray-2.2/pov/source\nOBJS=\"povray bezier blob bound boxes camera colour cones csg discs dump express gif gifdecod hfield iff image lighting matrices normal objects parse pigment planes point poly quadrics raw ray render spheres targa texture tokenize triangle txttest vect unix\"\nbuildtest() {\n  local label=\"$1\"; shift\n  local flags=\"$@\"\n  rm -f *.o\n  for o in $OBJS; do gcc -c -g $flags -o ${o}.o ${o}.c 2>/dev/null; done\n  OBJFILES=\"\"; for o in $OBJS; do OBJFILES=\"$OBJFILES ${o}.o\"; done\n  gcc -g $flags $OBJFILES -o ../bin/povtest -lm 2>/dev/null\n  local codes=\"\"\n  for i in 1 2 3; do\n    ../bin/povtest +L/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include +I/app/deps/illum1.pov +O/tmp/out.tga +W32 +H32 -V >/dev/null 2>&1\n    codes=\"$codes $?\"\n  done\n  echo \"[$label] flags='$flags' exits:$codes\"\n}\nbuildtest \"O2-no-fastmath\" -O2\nbuildtest \"O2-fastmath\" -O2 -ffast-math\nbuildtest \"O0\" -O0"
        }
      }
    },
    {
