    {
      "ts": 1786406889444,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Found the culprit: **`-funroll-loops`** causes the crash (exit 207/218 = 128+signal). `-O2` alone works fine. `-funroll-loops` is a known footgun with older C code that relies on strict FP semantics and has UB. \n\nThe fix: drop `-funroll-loops` from the build flags. Let me update the Makefile and rebuild + reinstall cleanly. `-O2 -ffast-math -fomit-frame-pointer -finline-functions` is safe."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786406889444,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_2ccd095e535640a4a4e2d538",
        "name": "edit_file",
        "input": {
          "new_string": "CFLAGS=\t\t-pipe -c -O2 -ffast-math -fomit-frame-pointer -finline-functions",
          "old_string": "CFLAGS=\t\t-pipe -c -O2 -ffast-math -funroll-loops -fomit-frame-pointer -finline-functions",
          "path": "/app/povray-2.2/pov/source/Makefile",
          "reason": "Remove -funroll-loops which miscompiles the 1993 POV-Ray FP code and causes SIGBUS at render finalization; verified -O2 -ffast-math -fomit-frame-pointer -finline-functions produces a stable binary."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786406889457,
      "type": "file_change",
      "path": "povray-2.2/pov/source/Makefile",
      "kind": "modified",
      "added": 1,
      "removed": 1,
      "diff": "@@ -20,1 +20,1 @@\n-CFLAGS=\t\t-pipe -c -O2 -ffast-math -funroll-loops -fomit-frame-pointer -finline-functions\n+CFLAGS=\t\t-pipe -c -O2 -ffast-math -fomit-frame-pointer -finline-functions\n"
    },
