      "ts": 1786407062159,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Done. POV-Ray 2.2 is built, installed, and verified working.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Built and installed POV-Ray 2.2** (`Persistence of Vision Raytracer Ver 2.2linux386`) to `/usr/local/bin/povray`.\n\n### What I did\n1. **Installed build tools** — `apt-get install build-essential zlib1g-dev unzip perl gdb` (the container had no compiler/make).\n2. **Found the source** — The official POV-Ray GitHub repo only has v3.x; POV-Ray 2.2 (1993) lives on **ibiblio's Linux archive** at `pub/Linux/apps/graphics/rays/pov/`. Downloaded four archives: `povsrc-2.2.tar.gz`, `povinc-2.2.tar.gz`, `povdoc-2.2.tar.gz`, `povscn-2.2.tar.gz`.\n3. **Extracted to `/app/povray-2.2`** — archives extract into a `pov/` subdir. I also created `povdoc/include/` (copied from `pov/include/`) because the sanity command's library path is `+L/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include`, and the scene needs `shapes.inc`, `colors.inc`, `textures.inc` there.\n4. **Built the \"standard\" (headless) target** — `povray.s`, which needs only `-lm` (no X11/svgalib).\n5. **Installed** via `make installs` → `/usr/local/bin/povray`.\n\n### Key fix: the 1993 source miscompiles under modern gcc\nThe original CFLAGS (`-m386 -ffast-math -funroll-loops ...`) caused a **SIGBUS crash (exit 138)** at the end of every render. I bisected it to **`-funroll-loops`** — it miscompiles the floating-point-heavy raytracing code. I also removed `-ffast-math` deliberately: it alters FP rounding and could shift pixel values, which matters for the reference-image comparison. Final working flags: **`-O2 -fomit-frame-pointer`** (pure IEEE math).\n\n### Verification\n- The exact sanity command `/usr/local/bin/povray +L/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include +I/app/deps/illum1.pov +O/dev/null +P -V` **completes successfully with exit code 0** and shows full rendering statistics (100×100, 91599 rays). Confirmed stable across 15 consecutive runs.\n- Rendering to a real file produces a valid 30018-byte TGA (100×100 @ 24bpp).\n- `/app/deps/illum1.pov` was **not modified** — it's actually POV-Ray 2.2's own sample scene (`scenes/level2/illum1.pov`)."
    },
