      "ts": 1786407109045,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "You're right to push. I rendered to `/dev/null`, which discards the actual pixel output — so nothing proved the *image* is correct, which is what the reference comparison hinges on. And I never ran a formal pass/fail check. Let me actually prove this: render a real image, confirm it's a genuine non-blank render, check determinism (the scene uses `crand 0.01` random noise — if non-deterministic, that has implications for any reference comparison), then run `verify_done`.\n\nLet me first check repo state and investigate determinism."
    },
