    {
      "ts": 1786407129792,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Two renders are byte-identical (same md5) — so despite `crand 0.01`, the render is **deterministic** with this build (POV-Ray 2.2 seeds its RNG deterministically). That's a strong positive sign for reference-image comparison.\n\nNow let me confirm the image is a genuine non-blank render (not all zeros/black), and check the color depth so I understand the output format."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786407129792,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_555ac17fee0242b981337474",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "echo \"=== Analyze rendered TGA pixel data (skip 18-byte header) ===\"\n# TGA is bottom-up, BGR. Check histogram of pixel bytes.\ntail -c +19 /tmp/r1.tga > /tmp/pixels.bin\necho \"pixel bytes: $(wc -c < /tmp/pixels.bin) (expect 30000 = 100*100*3)\"\necho \"=== non-zero bytes (proves it's not blank black) ===\"\nod -An -tu1 -v /tmp/pixels.bin | tr ' ' '\\n' | grep -v '^$' | sort -n | uniq -c | awk '{print $2, $1}' | sort -n > /tmp/hist.txt\necho \"distinct byte values: $(wc -l < /tmp/hist.txt)\"\necho \"zero bytes: $(grep -c '^0 ' /tmp/hist.txt)\"\necho \"=== min/max/mean ===\"\nawk '{n+=$2; if(min==\"\"||$1<min)min=$1; if($1>max)max=$1; sum+=$1*$2} END{printf \"min=%d max=%d mean=%.1f total_bytes=%d\\n\", min, max, sum/n, n}' /tmp/hist.txt\necho \"=== sample a few pixel values (bytes 1-12) ===\"\nod -An -tu1 -N12 /tmp/pixels.bin"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786407129815,
      "type": "tool_result",
      "call_id": "call_555ac17fee0242b981337474",
      "output": {
        "ok": {
          "content": "=== Analyze rendered TGA pixel data (skip 18-byte header) ===\npixel bytes: 30000 (expect 30000 = 100*100*3)\n=== non-zero bytes (proves it's not blank black) ===\ndistinct byte values: 256\nzero bytes: 1\n=== min/max/mean ===\nmin=0 max=255 mean=76.7 total_bytes=30000\n=== sample a few pixel values (bytes 1-12) ===\n  84  50  85  85  50  83  86  50  81  86  50  80\n\n[exit code: 0]"
